.TH FILEDIFFADVANCED 1
.SH NAME
filediffadvanced \- compare two files and report comparison time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B filediffadvanced
.RB [ \-b ]
.I LEFT RIGHT
.br
.B filediffadvanced \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B filediffadvanced
compares two regular files and reports whether they match.
By default it compares complete lines, including any terminating newline.
In binary mode it compares raw bytes.
Line and byte numbers start at 1.
If one file ends first, the command reports the first line or byte missing from it.
.PP
The command reports the size of each file in bytes and the elapsed time and CPU
time of the comparison in milliseconds.
The comparison stops at the first difference, so an early difference can take
less time than comparing two matching files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-b
Compare bytes instead of lines.
.TP
.B \-h
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The files match, or help was requested.
.TP
.B 1
The files differ.
.TP
.B 2
An argument or comparison error occurred.
.TP
.B 130
The user interrupted the comparison.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
filediffadvanced original.txt edited.txt
filediffadvanced \-b original.bin recovered.bin
.fi
